Subject: [PATCH 03/11] fix(sim): judge the first traverse of the rotary,
 multi-axis and cross-drill kinds

After a tool change the post sends Z, then X/Y at that height, then the
rotary words. The #2901 law skipped the rotary, multi-axis and
cross-drill kinds, so their first traverse posted unjudged.

- sim::verify::first_traverse_low_swept: a rotary kind reads its work
  and the steel that turns with it swept through a full turn about the
  fitted axis, the fixed steel as it stands, and the start at its
  machine height over the axis line.
- The multi-axis kinds and the cross drill on a mill answer to the
  #2901 tip law in the part frame.
- The op stamp of those kinds takes one more word, so a cache judged
  without the law reads Stale once.

Decision: docs/decisions/2965-first-traverse-rotary.md.

Fixes #2965

