From 05c9e56f271478eb03e5d9ee873822aa2bdedad3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:49:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] fix(app): read the table on a 3+2 plane only where the
 axial move can go under it

The 3+2 first-traverse law read the machine table's top face along the
tool axis. Along a horizontal axis (B 90) the table's far X edge read as
a high "top", so a B 90 pocket on tilthead.mch at clearance Z95 was
refused "under the fixture top Z625", and the multiaxis-indexed catalog
case "under the fixture top at Z500". A move along a horizontal axis
keeps the world Z: those refusals were false.

table_read now takes the worst start on the table top face and asks if
the move along the tool axis to the plane can drop the tool more than
Z_TOL under the table top. An up-pointing axis counts the table then
and names the top face's highest reading. A horizontal axis never
counts it. An axis that points down toward the table (past 90 deg) gets
a note, because the verdict can only say "raise", which is wrong there.

Pinned by first_traverse_table::a_horizontal_head_axis_does_not_read_the_far_table_edge,
::a_near_horizontal_head_axis_still_reads_the_table and
::a_head_tilt_past_90_names_the_table_unjudged (replaces the B 120 pin,
which read the wrong side of the face for such an axis).

Refs #2987

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
